{{Quote|I see Ben Quadinaros from the Tund system.|[[Fodesinbeed Annodue]]|audio=QuadinarosIntro.flac|<ref name="The Phantom Menace" />}}
The '''Tund system''',<ref name="Ben Quadinaros">{{Databank|ben-quadinaros|Ben Quadinaros}}</ref> also known as the '''Toong system''',<ref name="CompleteLocations">[[Star Wars: Complete Locations (2016)|''Star Wars: Complete Locations'']]</ref> was a mysterious [[star system]]<ref name="Ben Quadinaros" /> located in the [[Centrality]] [[sector]] of the [[Outer Rim Territories]]<ref name="TFABG" /> that contained the [[planet]] [[Tund]],<ref name="Complete Vehicles" /> a hidden world that became the [[Homeworld|home]] of<ref name="Tund System" /> a [[Toong]] [[Podracer]] [[Podracer (profession)|pilot]]<ref name="Ben Quadinaros" /> named [[Ben Quadinaros]].<ref name="Tund System" /> The Tund system lay in grid square U-8 of the [[Standard Galactic Grid]].<ref name="TFABG" />

==Behind the scenes==
The Tund system was first mentioned in the current ''[[Star Wars]]'' [[canon]] in the [[1999]] [[prequel trilogy]] film, [[Star Wars: Episode I The Phantom Menace|''Star Wars'': Episode I ''The Phantom Menace'']].<ref name="The Phantom Menace" /> It was then pictured on a [[Galaxy|galactic]] map included with the [[Star Wars: The Force Awakens Beginner Game|''Star Wars: The Force Awakens'' Beginner Game]], a [[roleplaying game]] produced by [[Fantasy Flight Games]] and released in [[2016]].<ref name="TFABG" /> The reference book [[Star Wars: Complete Locations (2016)|''Star Wars: Complete Locations'']], which also released in that year, introduced the name "Toong system" as an alternative to Tund system.<ref name="CompleteLocations" /> The [[StarWars.com]] [[Databank (2014-)|Databank]] erroneously refers to the Tund system as a world rather than a star system.<ref name="Tund System">{{Databank|tund-system|Tund System}}</ref>

The [[Tund system/Legends|system]] was first mentioned in the [[Star Wars Legends|''Star Wars'' Legends]] continuity in ''[[Lando Calrissian and the Mindharp of Sharu]]'', a [[1983]] novel written by [[L. Neil Smith]] as the first volume of the ''[[Star Wars: The Lando Calrissian Adventures]]'' trilogy.<ref name="Lando Calrissian and the Mindharp of Sharu">''[[Lando Calrissian and the Mindharp of Sharu]]''</ref>

